    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d239">

                <pb facs="0514" n="430" sameAs="frus:frus1886/pg430"/>

                <head>No. 235.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Sir L. West to Mr. Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >British Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1886-12-06"><hi rendition="#italic">December</hi> 6, 1886</date>.
                        [Received December 7.]</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to your note of the 27th of
                    October last, I have the honor to inclose herewith a certified copy of a report
                    of a committee <pb facs="0515" n="431" xml:id="pg431"/> of the privy council of
                    Canada, together with copy of the customs laws, which documents contain the
                    information required respecting the sale and exportation of fresh herring from
                    Grand Mandan Island.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>L. S. SACKVILLE WEST.</signed></closer>




